menu "Enclosure venting  (_MMU_VENT)"
  help
    Happy Hare enclosure venting macro configuration variables.

    The drying cycle calls heater_vent_macro (_MMU_VENT by default) every
    heater_vent_interval minutes. If the unit has a vent servo (MMU
    Features / Additions) the macro opens it, optionally runs the unit's
    managed fan, and closes the vent again after the vent time. Without a
    vent servo the macro only logs.

  comment "_"
  comment "_Vent servo"

  config VAR_VENT_SERVO_OPEN_ANGLE
    float "Servo open angle          "
    default 90
    help
      Vent servo angle with the vent open.

  config VAR_VENT_SERVO_CLOSED_ANGLE
    float "Servo closed angle        "
    default 0
    help
      Vent servo angle with the vent closed.

  config VAR_VENT_SERVO_DURATION
    float "Servo pulse duration (s)  "
    default 1.0
    help
      Duration in seconds of the PWM pulse train used to move the servo.
      The signal then stops so the servo doesn't jitter while held.

  comment "_"
  comment "_Venting"

  config VAR_VENT_DURATION
    float "Vent open time (s)        "
    default 10
    help
      How long the vent stays open each time it is opened.

  config VAR_VENT_RUN_FAN
    boolint "Run managed fan while open"
    default 1
    help
      Force the unit's managed fan on while the vent is open, then restore
      the mode it was in. Has no effect without a managed fan.

endmenu
